          "from_string": "Rendering\n\n1. Given the drawer is triggered, then it slides in from the right as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the drawer is open, then a backdrop overlay renders behind the panel covering the rest of the page.\n3. Given the drawer is open, then a close icon is visible in the top-right of the panel and closes the drawer on click.\n4. Given the drawer is open, then the tab navigation header renders with the correct tab labels as passed via props.\n5. Given a tab is active, then it renders in its selected state as defined in the design system.\n6. Given a tab is inactive, then it renders in its default state.\n7. Given a shopper clicks a tab, then that tab becomes active and the corresponding content area updates.\n\nBehaviour\n\n8. Given the drawer is open, then clicking the backdrop overlay closes the drawer.\n9. Given the drawer is open on mobile, then the panel renders full-width from the bottom or right as defined in the design system.\n10. Given the drawer content exceeds the panel height, then the content area scrolls independently without the tab header scrolling.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n11. Given no tab content is provided, then the drawer shell still renders without breaking layout.\n\nAccessibility\n\n12. Given the drawer opens, then focus moves to the drawer panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n13. Given the drawer closes, then focus returns to the trigger element that opened it.\n14. Given a keyboard user is within the drawer, then tabs are navigable via keyboard.\n15. The drawer has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n16. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA.",
          "to_string": "Rendering\n\n1. Given the drawer is triggered, then it slides in from the right as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the drawer is open, then a backdrop overlay renders behind the panel covering the rest of the page.\n3. Given the drawer is open, then a close icon is visible in the top-right of the panel and closes the drawer on click.\n4. Given the drawer is open, then the tab navigation header renders with the correct tab labels as passed via props.\n5. Given a tab is active, then it renders in its selected state as defined in the design system.\n6. Given a tab is inactive, then it renders in its default state.\n7. Given a shopper clicks a tab, then that tab becomes active and the corresponding content area updates.\n\nBehaviour\n\n8. Given the drawer is open, then clicking the backdrop overlay closes the drawer.\n9. Given the drawer is open on mobile, then the panel renders full-width from left to right but leaves a small piece of background open at the bottom as defined in the design system.\n10. Given the drawer content exceeds the panel height, then the content area scrolls independently without the tab header scrolling.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n11. Given no tab content is provided, then the drawer shell still renders without breaking layout.\n\nAccessibility\n\n12. Given the drawer opens, then focus moves to the drawer panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n13. Given the drawer closes, then focus returns to the trigger element that opened it.\n14. Given a keyboard user is within the drawer, then tabs are navigable via keyboard.\n15. The drawer has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n16. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA.",
